 him unless there are joined either as plaintiffs or as defendants all the surviving joint obligees. (2) Except in actions on negotiable instruments and except as stated in § 300, any joint obligee unless limited by agreement may sue in the name of all the joint obligees for the enforcement of the promise by a money judgment. § 294 RESTATEMENT OF CONTRACTS—SECOND"